 <title>A more perfect union?</title>
 <link>https://coveredinbees.org.archived.website/node/237</link>
 <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.nytimes.com/2008/06/03/us/politics/03text-obama.html?fta=y&amp;amp;pagewanted=print&quot;&gt;Obama wins the democratic nomination&lt;/a&gt; and ends his first speech as nominee thus:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;cite&gt;Now, the other side will come here in September and offer a very different set of policies and positions, and that is a good thing. That is a debate I look forward to. It is a debate that the American people deserve on the issues that will help determine the future of this country and the future for our children.&lt;/cite&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;cite&gt;But what you don&#039;t deserve is another election that&#039;s governed by fear, and innuendo, and division. What you won&#039;t hear from this campaign or this party is the kind of politics that uses religion as a wedge and patriotism as a bludgeon. What you won&#039;t see from this campaign or this party is a politics that sees our opponents not as competitors to challenge, but enemies to polarize, because we may call ourselves Democrats and Republicans, but we are Americans first. We are always Americans first.&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://coveredinbees.org.archived.website/node/237&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;read more&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
